    <string name="help_title">How to use</string>
    <string name="help_body" formatted="false">Kausar Recorder is developed by Alkausar. Record screen and voice with audio effects.

=== RECORDING TYPE ===
• Screen recording: capture the phone display (needs screen capture permission).
• Voice recording: audio only, no video.

=== MICROPHONE / AUDIO SOURCE ===
• Microphone only: phone mic.
• Internal audio: sound from other apps (Android 10+).
• Internal + microphone: both mixed.
• Screen + microphone: screen video with mic audio.

=== FORMAT ===
• AAC (.m4a): smaller files, good for long-term storage.
• WAV (.wav): higher quality; used automatically when effects are on.

=== AUDIO EFFECTS ===
• Studio: clean sound, no effect.
• Flanger: light modulation.
• Echo: clear single echo.
• Reverb (V8): multi-tap stereo reverb like a V8 sound card.

=== SLIDERS ===
• Microphone strength: 100%% is normal; raise if quiet, lower if clipping.
• Noise level: amount of soft noise when noise mode is on (0%% = off).

=== CHECKBOXES ===
• Force stereo: on = convert mono to wide stereo; off = keep mono.
• Noise mode: on = soft Windows-like noise floor; off = no noise.
• Skip silence: on = skip very quiet parts (smaller files); off = record everything.
• Dynamic gain (AGC): on = boost quiet speech; off = fixed volume.

=== BUTTONS ===
• Start recording: begin a session.
• Stop: end and open Save / Play / Share dialog.
• Add bookmark: mark a timestamp while recording.
• Settings: change app language.
• Read guide: show this help.
• Refresh list: reload saved files.

=== NOTIFICATION ===
While recording, use the notification for Pause / Resume / Stop without opening the app.

=== STORAGE ===
Files go under KausarRecorder:
• Music/KausarRecorder/Audio — voice
• Movies/KausarRecorder/Screen — screen</string>
